>This is carry over / steal from the frp Dungeons + Dragons, where
>after a polymorph or resurrection, or other nasty happening,
>you have to make a kind of 'saving throw' to see whether your body
>survived the shock that it has just undergone, with failure
>resulting in death.  I would assume that Hack rolls a system shock
>everytime you get polymorphed, and you just got unlucky that time.

Close, but not close enough.

The system shock check in Nethack depends on luck; high enough luck and
you never get one.  With a ring of polymorph control you also never get one.

System shock in Nethack does not result in death, but in 1-30 points of damage.
If you have >30 points, or if you're already polymorphed (and thus one
quantity of damage cannot kill you but will at most return you to human), it
cannot kill you.
